# Radial Bar Chart (`chart-radial-bars`)

Concentric gauge-shaped radial bars: rings sweep in one after another when visible; hovering or focusing a ring brightens it, dims the others and swaps the centre readout.

## What it should do
Build radial bars: for each item an arc from 135° sweeping 270°·value/max (track + value path, round caps), radius decreasing per ring; animate pathLength with a stagger when in view; hovering/focusing a ring (or its legend button) dims the others, thickens it with a glow and shows its value in the centre.

## Project requirements
- React 19 + TypeScript, Tailwind CSS v4, shadcn/ui-style CSS variables (`background`, `foreground`, `muted`, `muted-foreground`, `border`, `card`, `primary`, `ring`). If the project lacks shadcn, set it up first (`npx shadcn@latest init`).
- Animation engine: **motion**.
- Install dependencies: `npm i motion`
- Put the component at `components/kinetik/chart-radial-bars.tsx`.
- `cn` lives at `lib/kinetik/utils.ts` (source below).
- Shared hooks go at `lib/kinetik/core.ts` (source below).

## Non-negotiables
- **Accessibility:** A legend of buttons doubles as the accessible value list and focus target. Reduced motion: static rings.
- **Performance:** pathLength per ring; hover only toggles opacity/stroke.
- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion` (replace movement with opacity or an instant change).
- Animate only transform / opacity / filter / clip-path. No hard-coded theme colors — use CSS variables so it works in light and dark.

